  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Conceived and executed by Robin Price in collaboration with Emily K. Larned ... Mostly excerpted from previously published books ... Ten different artists ... contributed original artwork ... The first and last sections of the book are collated consistently throughout the edition; the middle four signatures vary. Each copy is unique ... In an edition of 60 letter-press copies" -- colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Bound by Emily K. Larned, the book is sewn onto cords attached to sanded plexiglas covers" and laid into a larger (28 cm.) box with wooden inserts to hold the book firmly in place.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="505" ind1="0" ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">19 July 2000 / Robin Price -- Matsuo Basho / Hiroaki Sato -- 36 Mesostics re and not re Duchamp / John Cage -- Dada &amp; Chance / Hans Richter --Library of Babel / Roderick V. Jenen -- [Poems] / Fujiwara no Teika &amp; Fujiwara no Ietaka -- Tea ceremony / Leonard Koren -- Chance assignment / John gilgun -- Imperfect irregular beauty / Hara Kōshirō -- Exquisite corpse / Uwe m. Schneed -- -- Elevator here at the Gramercy Park Hotel / Alvin Lucier -- In Japan / Shurryu Suzuki -- Friendship quilts / Susan McKelvey -- Quotes on 'Palimpsest' / [various writers] -- John Cage / Anne Harnoncourt -- John Cage / Mark Sweed -- Proof, run-in sheets, run-ups / Geoffrey Ashall Glaister -- Few examples / Paul Klee.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="520" ind1="8" ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Contains the work of 10 artists, working independently, on previously printed &amp; technically annotated sheets with new text imprinted on similarly used sheets which are interspersed with the artists' works.</subfield>
  </datafield>
